Experiment 7(a): Write a shell script and a C program to perform the following string operations: (To extract a substring and length from a given string)
(b) To find the length of a given string.
Compare the running time using time command.  


Steps:
Open the Terminal.  
Create a shell script using nano expt7a.sh.  
Write a shell script to extract a substring and find its length.  
Save the file and execute it using bash expt7a.sh.  
Measure execution time using time bash expt7a.sh.  
Create a C program file using nano expt7a.c.  
Write the C program to perform both string operations: substring extraction and string length calculation.  
Save and compile: gcc expt7a.c -o expt7a.  
Execute the C program using ./expt7a.  
Measure execution time using time ./expt7a.  
Compare the execution times of the shell script and C program using the same input string.
